1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,201
If you work for yourself in Germany,

2
00:00:06,201 --> 00:00:08,732
as a Freiberufler or with a small Gewerbe,

3
00:00:08,732 --> 00:00:10,493
you know the paperwork.

4
00:00:10,493 --> 00:00:14,730
Before your first invoice, there's a tax registration questionnaire.

5
00:00:14,730 --> 00:00:17,812
Then come invoices with mandatory details, receipts,

6
00:00:17,812 --> 00:00:19,628
bank statements, tax returns,

7
00:00:19,628 --> 00:00:21,554
and letters from the Finanzamt,

8
00:00:21,554 --> 00:00:24,360
often in a language that isn't your first.

9
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:27,222
I wanted an assistant that helps with all of it,

10
00:00:27,222 --> 00:00:29,643
one clear step at a time, without pretending

11
00:00:29,643 --> 00:00:31,239
to be a tax adviser.

12
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:33,440
So I built German Business Kit.

13
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:38,299
German Business Kit is a set of seven skills for Claude and Codex.

14
00:00:38,299 --> 00:00:40,409
A skill is a package of instructions,

15
00:00:40,409 --> 00:00:42,930
references and templates that the assistant loads

16
00:00:42,930 --> 00:00:44,783
when your request needs it.

17
00:00:44,783 --> 00:00:46,841
So there's no new app to learn.

18
00:00:46,841 --> 00:00:49,620
You work in Claude Code, the Claude app, or Codex,

19
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:52,553
and you ask in plain English, German or Russian.

20
00:00:52,553 --> 00:00:54,920
Guides and reports come in all three.

21
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:58,428
Every task follows the same rhythm.

22
00:00:58,428 --> 00:01:00,707
One: you ask in your own words.

23
00:01:00,707 --> 00:01:05,096
For example: help me turn these agreed terms into a German proposal.

24
00:01:05,096 --> 00:01:07,262
Two: the assistant clarifies.

25
00:01:07,262 --> 00:01:09,826
It reuses facts you've already confirmed,

26
00:01:09,826 --> 00:01:11,707
asks only for what's missing,

27
00:01:11,707 --> 00:01:15,354
then prepares a readable draft and names the next step.

28
00:01:15,354 --> 00:01:17,976
Three: for ongoing work, it saves results,

29
00:01:17,976 --> 00:01:19,914
confirmed facts and open questions

30
00:01:19,914 --> 00:01:22,251
in your private business folder.

31
00:01:22,251 --> 00:01:26,240
Next month, it continues from there instead of starting over.

32
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:30,240
The skills follow the life of a sole trader.

33
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:32,673
Start helps you describe your activity,

34
00:01:32,673 --> 00:01:35,503
work out whether it's Freiberufler or Gewerbe,

35
00:01:35,503 --> 00:01:38,050
and prepare registration worksheets.

36
00:01:38,050 --> 00:01:42,578
Operations handles proposals, invoices, payment follow-ups and letters.

37
00:01:42,578 --> 00:01:45,465
Accounting organizes receipts and bank exports,

38
00:01:45,465 --> 00:01:47,502
matches them, and prepares the month

39
00:01:47,502 --> 00:01:51,464
in the system you choose, including software you already use.

40
00:01:51,464 --> 00:01:54,011
Tax researches the rules for your period,

41
00:01:54,011 --> 00:01:56,331
makes estimates with recorded checks,

42
00:01:56,331 --> 00:01:59,274
and prepares returns and Finanzamt replies.

43
00:01:59,274 --> 00:02:02,501
Services compares banks, insurance and software.

44
00:02:02,501 --> 00:02:06,802
Changes plans a second activity, a first hire, a pause, or closing.

45
00:02:06,802 --> 00:02:11,160
And the main kit skill is the front door that routes mixed requests.

46
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:14,930
Your business folder keeps everything together

47
00:02:14,930 --> 00:02:18,242
in five everyday areas: inbox, documents, accounts,

48
00:02:18,242 --> 00:02:19,928
taxes and business.

49
00:02:19,928 --> 00:02:22,698
Originals are preserved and numbered.

50
00:02:22,698 --> 00:02:25,889
One profile covers all your activities and years,

51
00:02:25,889 --> 00:02:28,900
and an overview page shows where you are.

52
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:31,911
The kit can also make a full, verified backup,

53
00:02:31,911 --> 00:02:34,560
and restore it into a new location.

54
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:38,257
Here's what that looks like in the real apps.

55
00:02:38,257 --> 00:02:41,403
In Codex, the kit shows up as seven skills in your project,

56
00:02:41,403 --> 00:02:44,200
each with a plain description of what it's for.

57
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:47,742
In Claude, you ask in your own words.

58
00:02:47,742 --> 00:02:50,726
In this fictional example, a creator makes videos,

59
00:02:50,726 --> 00:02:53,600
and the first brands want to pay for posts.

60
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:57,613
Instead of a lecture, you get one small first step,

61
00:02:57,613 --> 00:03:00,680
and only the three questions needed to take it.

62
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:06,680
And it works in German, too: the same skills, the same private folder.

63
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:11,237
Now some real questions, each asked in a fresh session

64
00:03:11,237 --> 00:03:12,935
with the released kit.

65
00:03:12,935 --> 00:03:14,687
A translator in Berlin asks:

66
00:03:14,687 --> 00:03:16,494
Freiberufler or Gewerbe?

67
00:03:16,494 --> 00:03:19,397
The answer quotes the law that names translators,

68
00:03:19,397 --> 00:03:22,190
explains the one registration needed through ELSTER

69
00:03:22,190 --> 00:03:23,887
and its one-month deadline,

70
00:03:23,887 --> 00:03:26,680
and links to the official pages it opened.

71
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:32,825
A web designer in Hamburg asks about the small business VAT exemption.

72
00:03:32,825 --> 00:03:35,300
The answer explains the first-year limit,

73
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:37,665
what happens when a payment crosses it,

74
00:03:37,665 --> 00:03:39,700
and when regular VAT starts.

75
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:42,945
And when the Finance Ministry's guidance wouldn't load,

76
00:03:42,945 --> 00:03:45,200
it said so, instead of guessing.

77
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,885
A photographer in Munich, whose profit dropped,

78
00:03:49,885 --> 00:03:52,486
asks about quarterly tax prepayments.

79
00:03:52,486 --> 00:03:54,466
The answer estimates the likely tax

80
00:03:54,466 --> 00:03:57,860
with this year's tariff, checks the arithmetic two ways,

81
00:03:57,860 --> 00:04:00,970
flags that the next payment is due in fifteen days,

82
00:04:00,970 --> 00:04:04,760
and drafts the German letter, marked as a draft, not sent.

83
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:11,818
One principle runs through the whole kit: it prepares, you decide and send.

84
00:04:11,818 --> 00:04:15,251
Extraction, proposal, review, booking, authorization,

85
00:04:15,251 --> 00:04:18,924
submission and the authority's answer are separate steps,

86
00:04:18,924 --> 00:04:21,092
each with its own evidence.

87
00:04:21,092 --> 00:04:24,765
A polished draft is never treated as a filed return.

88
00:04:24,765 --> 00:04:26,692
You sign in to ELSTER, your bank

89
00:04:26,692 --> 00:04:29,161
or your accounting software yourself,

90
00:04:29,161 --> 00:04:32,232
you never type passwords or TANs into the chat,

91
00:04:32,232 --> 00:04:34,520
and you make the final click.

92
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:37,653
Installing takes a few minutes.

93
00:04:37,653 --> 00:04:40,427
In the Claude app, open Customize, then Plugins,

94
00:04:40,427 --> 00:04:42,347
add the marketplace from GitHub,

95
00:04:42,347 --> 00:04:44,533
and install German Business Kit.

96
00:04:44,533 --> 00:04:46,827
In Claude Code, it's two commands.

97
00:04:46,827 --> 00:04:50,453
In Codex, the released skills are copied into your project.

98
00:04:50,453 --> 00:04:53,067
Or paste the install request from the README,

99
00:04:53,067 --> 00:04:55,467
and let your assistant do the setup.

100
00:04:55,467 --> 00:04:59,040
Then start a fresh chat, and say: start the welcome setup.

101
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,636
A few honest limits.

102
00:05:01,636 --> 00:05:03,507
This is an early preview.

103
00:05:03,507 --> 00:05:06,369
It's AI assistance, not professional tax advice,

104
00:05:06,369 --> 00:05:09,506
and AI can get calculations and deadlines wrong.

105
00:05:09,506 --> 00:05:13,909
It doesn't send anything to ELSTER, and it isn't a complete tax engine.

106
00:05:13,909 --> 00:05:17,486
Whatever the assistant reads is processed by its AI provider,

107
00:05:17,486 --> 00:05:19,743
so start with a made-up example.

108
00:05:19,743 --> 00:05:22,439
The kit is open source under the MIT licence,

109
00:05:22,439 --> 00:05:24,861
and the link is in the description.

110
00:05:24,861 --> 00:05:29,484
If you run a small business in Germany, try it, and tell me what's missing.

111
00:05:29,484 --> 00:05:31,080
Danke, and bis bald.
